<SPT><TTL>QUALITY ASSURANCE</TTL><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<SPT><TTL>Design Conditions</TTL><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<TXT>Design must be as specified in Section <SRF>33 52 43.11</SRF> AVIATION FUEL MECHANICAL EQUIPMENT.  Components must be <RID>ASME B16.5</RID>
 Class 150 (<MET>9 MPa</MET><ENG> 275 psig</ENG> at<MET> 38 degrees C</MET><ENG> 100 degrees F</ENG>, except that swivel joints and pressure fueling nozzles 
must be<MET> 824 kPa</MET><ENG> 125 psig</ENG> at<MET> 58 degrees C</MET><ENG> 100 degrees F</ENG>).  Nominal diameters must be as follows:</TXT><BRK/>
<TXT><TAB HEADERROWS="0">
<WBK>
   <STS/>
   <TDA COLUMNCOUNT="2" ROWCOUNT="8">
      <COL AUTOWIDTH="0" WIDTH="216.75"/>
      <COL AUTOWIDTH="0" WIDTH="240.00"/>
